commit aa77a3dc9cebe31f1b2d8cbfea873cee3cb31603

C03: a verified capture is reported in the first person without its identifiers (SCREEN1401)

SCREEN1399 measured «sacá un screenshot» on the reviewed capture: the capture was approved, completed and verified in every case, but the literal published an imperative echo of the order («Sacá un screenshot del área virtual.») and three variants published nothing because every draft narrated the capture identifier (captureId, sha256 exposed by the situation payload) and the internal-code veto blocked them with no retry hint.

llm._compose_situation_payload: for capture.screenshot and capture.active.window the payload projects only what the person can use: the dimensions, what was captured (the whole screen or the active window, in the response language) and that it stayed private; captureId, sha256 and the timestamp stay in the receipt.
llm._payload_fact_defect: capture_not_reported when a verified capture's final has no first-person past report (saqué, tomé, capturé, hice, took, captured…) or opens by repeating the order; its retry hint asks for the first-person report without identifiers and without inventing where the file went.

No .NET change. Offline probe only; tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


